				<div class="mt-include" id="s162885"><p class="lt-chem-162885">We can separate an analyte and an interferent if there is a significant difference in at least one of their chemical or physical properties. Table 7.6.1
 provides a partial list of separation techniques, organized by the chemical or physical property affecting the separation.</p>

